0090:     - The most numerous non-background color forms stationary grey obstacle pixels.
0091:     - The other two colors form a single 3x3 top-edge marker whose top two rows
0092:       are maroon and whose bottom row contains maroon or blue control pixels.
0093: 
0094:     Rule
0095:     - Erase the top marker.
0096:     - Treat each marker column as a vertical drop retaining its three colors.
0097:     - A column whose bottom control pixel is blue stops immediately above the
0098:       first grey pixel below that column, or bottom-aligns if none exists.
0099:     - Contiguous maroon-ended columns pass through obstacles and bottom-align;
0100:       if such a run has a clear down-right slide from a grey ledge, shift the
0101:       run one column right before bottom-aligning.
0102:     - When a maroon-ended drop lands through a grey bar on the bottom edge, clear
0103:       the rest of the marker-width gap in that bottom bar.
0104: 
0105:     Key insight
0106:     - The bottom row of the top marker is a control strip: blue cells mean
0107:       "stick to the first obstacle," while maroon cells mean "fall through."
