0047:     - Each plus is a 4-connected object with a 3x3 bbox and pixels at the center plus the four cardinal neighbors.
0048:     - Some plus centers share an unobstructed diagonal line of background cells.
0049: 
0050:     Rule
0051:     - Keep every input pixel unchanged.
0052:     - For each pair of plus centers with equal row and column separation, scan the straight diagonal segment between them.
0053:     - If every interior cell on that diagonal segment is background, recolor those interior cells red.
0054: 
0055:     Key insight
0056:     - The added pixels are not extensions of plus arms; they are the empty center-to-center diagonal gaps between aligned plus objects.
